+7. GROUP: KVM_S390_VM_ARCH_MODE
+===============================
+
+:Architectures: s390
+
+7.1. ATTRIBUTE: KVM_S390_VM_ARCH_MODE_CURRENT (r/w)
+---------------------------------------------------
+
+The architectural mode of the configuration, available with
+KVM_CAP_S390_ESA390_CM enabled.
+
+:Parameters: address of a buffer in user space (u32) with one of
+
+	     ==============================  ==================================
+	     KVM_S390_ARCH_MODE_ZARCH        z/Architecture architectural mode
+	     KVM_S390_ARCH_MODE_ESA390_CM    ESA/390-compatibility mode
+	     ==============================  ==================================
+
+:Returns:   -ENXIO if the capability is not enabled;
+	    -EFAULT if the given address is not accessible from kernel space;
+	    -EINVAL for an unknown mode, or to enter the
+	    ESA/390-compatibility mode while guest debugging is enabled for a
+	    vCPU;
+	    -EBUSY if a vCPU is running or executes another ioctl;
+	    0 in case of success.
+
+Setting the attribute changes the mode of all vCPUs. It only switches the
+way KVM runs the vCPUs and presents interruptions. The effects on register
+contents that the architecture defines for a change of the mode (for a
+reset that belongs to a load, or for the SIGP set-architecture order) have
+to be applied by user space, see KVM_CAP_S390_ESA390_CM in
+Documentation/virt/kvm/api.rst. KVM aligns the prefix of every vCPU to the
+prefix area of the new mode and changes facility bit 2 (z/Architecture
+architectural mode active) in the facility list of the VM; all other facility
+bits are left to user space.
